    points: ['Each extra appliance after two: £20', 'Certificate emailed the same day', 'Free reminder next year'] },
  { id: 'combined', tier: 'Best value', popular: true, name: 'Gas safety certificate + boiler service', price: '£199', unit: 'one visit, inc VAT',
    points: ['Save £21 on booking them apart', 'Keeps the boiler warranty valid', 'Both records emailed the same day'] },
  { id: 'portfolio', tier: 'Landlords and agents', name: '3 or more properties', price: '£80', unit: 'per certificate, inc VAT',
    points: ['Save £20 on every certificate', 'We arrange access with tenants', 'Renewal dates tracked for you'] },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Is a gas safe certificate the same as a gas safety certificate?', a: 'Yes. People call it a gas safe certificate, a landlord gas safety record or a CP12. They all mean the same yearly check, done by a Gas Safe registered engineer. In Liverpool ours costs £100 for up to two appliances.' },
  { q: 'How much is a gas safety certificate in Liverpool?', a: 'With us it is £100 including VAT for up to two gas appliances, usually the boiler and hob, and £20 for each extra appliance, such as a gas cooker. A certificate and a boiler service together are £199. Landlords with 3 or more properties pay £80 per certificate.' },
  { q: 'How long does a gas safety check take?', a: 'Most flats and houses take under an hour. A home with a boiler and a gas hob is often done in 30 to 45 minutes.' },
  { q: 'Do landlords need a gas safety certificate every year?', a: 'Yes. Every gas appliance you provide must be checked every 12 months. You can have the check done up to 2 months early and keep the same renewal date.' },
  { q: 'Can I get a free gas safety check?', a: 'Some people can, from their energy supplier, for example if they are on the Priority Services Register and meet the supplier rules. This is for your own home. It does not replace the yearly landlord certificate. Ask your supplier.' },
  { q: 'Do homeowners need a gas safety certificate?', a: 'Not by law. If you own and live in your home, you do not need one. But a yearly boiler service or gas safety check is a good idea, and buyers often ask for one when you sell.' },
  { q: 'Do I need to be there?', a: 'No. Many landlords are not. We can arrange a time with your tenant or letting agent, and email the certificate to you afterwards.' },
  { q: 'What if my tenant will not let you in?', a: 'Keep a record of every attempt to get access, such as texts and emails. The law expects you to take reasonable steps. We will try again at a time that suits the tenant, and we can give you a note of each missed visit.' },
  { q: 'Can I renew early without losing months?', a: 'Yes. If the check is done up to 2 months before the old certificate runs out, the new one keeps the old expiry date. You do not lose any time.' },
  { q: 'Do I pay if something fails?', a: 'Yes, the check is still paid for, because the engineer has done the work. If something needs fixing, we tell you the price before we do it. Once it is safe, we issue the certificate.' },
  { q: 'Do you check gas fires?', a: 'No. Our certificate covers boilers, gas cookers and hobs. If a property has a gas fire, it needs an engineer registered for gas fires, or we can disconnect and cap it safely.' },
  { q: 'Is a gas safety certificate the same as a boiler service?', a: 'No. The certificate checks that every gas appliance is safe to use. A service cleans and checks the boiler inside, so it keeps working well and keeps its warranty. Many landlords book both in one visit for £199.' },
  { q: 'Do I need a carbon monoxide alarm?', a: 'In a rented home, yes. Since October 2022, landlords must fit a carbon monoxide alarm in any room with a fixed fuel-burning appliance, such as a gas boiler. Gas cookers are not included. We check the alarm works during the visit.' },
  { q: 'Do I need a certificate to sell my house?', a: 'It is not a legal must for a home you live in. But many buyers and their solicitors ask for one, and it can stop a sale being held up. The same check works for this.' },
  { q: 'Can I get a certificate today?', a: 'Often, yes, when we have a free slot. Call 0151 558 0334 to check. The certificate is emailed the same day.' },
  { q: 'Are you Gas Safe registered?', a: 'Yes. Gas work is done by our Gas Safe registered engineers. You can check any engineer on the Gas Safe Register before they start.' },
];
